# Two parameters of one family are two values: `report(c: Circle, q: Square)` takes a Circle and a Square, each by the
# name that holds it, also once their family closes them into one box. A route's parameters are values with their
# names at the route's start: its own arrow takes them, and a step handed one by its name takes the same value.

route shapes.report
step report/show_circle
step report/show_square

line entry > report call
line Circle·c > report value
line Square·q > report value
line Circle·c > report/show_circle value
line Square·q > report/show_square value
line report/show_circle > Screen own
line report/show_square > Screen own

home Circle·c report
home Square·q report

side entry left
side Screen right

# A list of a type holds values of it: `total(shapes: list[Shape])` takes Shapes.
route shapes.total
line entry > total call
line Shape·shapes > total value

home Shape·shapes total

side entry left
